# Design system

Use tokens in `src/styles/global.css` and layout primitives before inventing new visual patterns.

Do not produce generic AI aesthetics.

Avoid:

- Giant gradient heroes, glassmorphism, blobs, purple SaaS palettes
- Identical 3-column card grids, logo clouds, meaningless stats
- Every section centered or wrapped in a card
- Excessive radius, shadows, pills, or animation

Prefer:

- Strong typography and whitespace
- Asymmetric or editorial compositions
- Section-to-section variation that matches the business
- Real or abstract architectural imagery, not stock-photo heroes

Example:

```astro
<!-- ❌ -->
<section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-500 to-blue-500 py-32 text-center">
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3">{/* three identical cards */}</div>
</section>

<!-- ✅ -->
<Section>
  <Split>
    <h1>…</h1>
    <p>…</p>
  </Split>
</Section>
```

When adding a component, first check whether an existing one already solves it.
